      "title": "A product name is not the whole promise",
      "narration": "Rosa compares three ways an annuity can develop value. One credits interest declared by the insurer. Another uses selected investment portfolios. A third calculates interest using a market index and a contract formula. The key question is who bears the investment risk and exactly what is guaranteed. Income timing is a different classification: fixed, indexed or variable describes the design, while immediate or deferred describes when income starts. An early withdrawal can also produce a market value adjustment under some contracts. Keep the source of growth, minimum promise, withdrawal rules and selected income benefit separate when comparing these choices.",
